{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MJ3diTUXxRDtwfHPN7U97R","type":"tool_result","content":"commit ae10e947e6f3a7fd1ff5d17a61a462a6cb210b40\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 10:36:11 2026 +0200\n\n    smoke/proxy: podman run -i so heredocs reach python3 - (inbox 49)\n    \n    Without -i podman never attaches stdin, so the heredoc programs piped to\n    python3 - read an empty script and exit 0 having done nothing; run-smoke's\n    trailing validator then fails on the absent receipt. Present in all four\n    revisions of the podman line; found by the cp-smoke steward with an\n    in-container repro. Same defect fixed preemptively in make-proxy.sh:116\n    before cp-proxy could hit it.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RZLdMFrCnEgtaWKRfxfWWP\n\n scripts/make-proxy.sh | 2 +-\n scripts/run-smoke.sh  | 2 +-\n 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n=== worklist grep ===\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\n - container-recipe | Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\n - instruments | Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay (rev 2: lineage carrier for ae10e94)\n - host-tooling | Pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner\n - bench-harness | Measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix\n - proxy-tooling | Proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner (rev 2: latch cleared)\n - morning-ledger | Archive the stop-state, then render the morning ledger and the announcement draft\n - catalog-handoff | Prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator\n - rdma-package | Close the RDMA package: the missing pin test plus the odinlink and kernel-truth folds\n - cp-weights | Checkpoint: re-stage the workload checkpoint onto both nodes (2026-08-30 revision: the fleet's local-models sync pruned both staged trees on 08-29 — the artifact has no catalog row — so this must re-copy ~185.6 GB per node; runs after the attended co [rev 2: validate-only]\n - cp-build | Checkpoint: the container engine build\n - cp-smoke | Checkpoint: in-container smoke — identity, fp8 cast, admission\n - cp-proxy | Checkpoint: proxy checkpoint first light, single node\n - cp-tp2 | Checkpoint: pair first light, residency, fidelity, full context\n - cp-bench | Checkpoint: the counterbalanced bench matrix\n - cp-close | Checkpoint: full verification pass over everything the night produced\n - usb4stream-bench | Author the wedge-safe stream-primitive first-light bench, its receipts bound, and the transport decision memo\n - cp-usb4stream | Checkpoint: single-open stream-primitive first light (dead-last; runs only when the serve is already down — a live pair on the shared cable is a typed skip; one open attempt ever; never a fail-status receipt)\n - rocm10-probe | Measure ROCm 10.0.0 viability on a separate image tag, off the critical path, after the bench","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"639c4953-ad0e-42b0-9626-a9206714b3c7","uuid":"7f48b11a-2533-4c59-915e-7502ecc92eff","timestamp":"2026-08-30T09:16:16.491Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit ae10e947e6f3a7fd1ff5d17a61a462a6cb210b40\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 10:36:11 2026 +0200\n\n    smoke/proxy: podman run -i so heredocs reach python3 - (inbox 49)\n    \n    Without -i podman never attaches stdin, so the heredoc programs piped to\n    python3 - read an empty script and exit 0 having done nothing; run-smoke's\n    trailing validator then fails on the absent receipt. Present in all four\n    revisions of the podman line; found by the cp-smoke steward with an\n    in-container repro. Same defect fixed preemptively in make-proxy.sh:116\n    before cp-proxy could hit it.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/s