{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Hxrme6d7pkJJEDRZAFvLr","type":"tool_result","content":"237d508 NOT ancestor\n---\ncommit 237d5081476bf47530ea45077e07914cd7464d57\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 11:13:53 2026 +0200\n\n    make-proxy: three first-run fixes against the real workload\n    \n    1. read_header unwraps the fork's parse_safetensors_header tuple\n       (metadata, data_offset) instead of iterating the tuple.\n    2. The engram table lives on whichever layer carries the shards (layer 1\n       in this checkpoint, 128 shards) — key off the first shard-bearing\n       layer instead of hardcoding layer 0.\n    3. discover_shards yields _LayerShards dataclasses; verify against their\n       .shards dict keys, not the dataclass itself.\n    \n    All three found by dry-running the build locally; it now completes:\n    4.66 GB proxy, 725 tensors, header-only reads, manifest written.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RZLdMFrCnEgtaWKRfxfWWP\n\n scripts/make-proxy.sh | 18 +++++++++++++-----\n 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n=== branches containing 237d508 ===\n+ main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/main","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"639c4953-ad0e-42b0-9626-a9206714b3c7","uuid":"063e78a0-ccf9-487f-b5cb-88c15788eaf5","timestamp":"2026-08-30T09:16:30.327Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"237d508 NOT ancestor\n---\ncommit 237d5081476bf47530ea45077e07914cd7464d57\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 11:13:53 2026 +0200\n\n    make-proxy: three first-run fixes against the real workload\n    \n    1. read_header unwraps the fork's parse_safetensors_header tuple\n       (metadata, data_offset) instead of iterating the tuple.\n    2. The engram table lives on whichever layer carries the shards (layer 1\n       in this checkpoint, 128 shards) — key off the first shard-bearing\n       layer instead of hardcoding layer 0.\n    3. discover_shards yields _LayerShards dataclasses; verify against their\n       .shards dict keys, not the dataclass itself.\n    \n    All three found by dry-running the build locally; it now completes:\n    4.66 GB proxy, 725 tensors, header-only reads, manifest written.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RZLdMFrCnEgtaWKRfxfWWP\n\n scripts/make-proxy.sh | 18 +++++++++++++-----\n 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n=== branches containing 237d508 ===\n+ main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/main","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
